  "tips_studio_guide_1": "Press Ctrl+Enter to generate once your prompt is ready. Results spread across this canvas batch by batch: middle-drag or Shift+left-drag to pan, Ctrl+scroll to zoom, and WASD to move around.",
  "@tips_studio_guide_1": {
    "description": "Shortcut generateImage (ctrl+enter); canvas controls from settings_outputViewer_canvasDescription."
  },
  "tips_studio_guide_2": "Write your go-to artist strings, quality tags and composition notes once, save them as blocks, and pull them from the block library next time. Blocks are more than copy-paste: set them to Fixed, Sequential or Random draw and every generation gets a new combination.",
  "@tips_studio_guide_2": {
    "description": "Pill instance modes (pillSettingsModeFixed / Sequential / Random)."
  },
  "tips_studio_guide_3": "Got a random roll you love? Lock it, then re-roll the other blocks. Locked blocks stay put while the rest keeps shuffling — perfect for \"keep this pose, try a few more outfits.\"",
  "@tips_studio_guide_3": {
    "description": "pillCardLock / pillCardReroll."
  },
  "tips_studio_guide_4": "Drag an image into the window and you'll be asked how to use it: Image2Image, Vibe Transfer, Precise Reference, or just extracting its prompt and settings. If it carries NovelAI metadata, one drag shows exactly how it was made.",
  "@tips_studio_guide_4": {
    "description": "Image drop dialog (drop_dialogTitle)."
  },
  "tips_studio_guide_5": "A character box is really a placement box. Besides people, you can put a cat, a lamp or a shop sign in one. Switch Position to Custom and drag its anchor on the preview to tell the model where it belongs.",
  "@tips_studio_guide_5": {
    "description": "Character position canvas (characterCanvas_custom, characterCanvas_dragHint)."
  },
  "tips_studio_guide_6": "Select part of a prompt and hold Alt while scrolling to adjust its weight. Without Alt the wheel just scrolls, so weights never change by accident. You can switch the modifier to Ctrl in Settings.",
  "@tips_studio_guide_6": {
    "description": "Weight scroll modifier (settings_enablePromptWeightScrollSubtitle)."
  },
  "tips_studio_guide_7": "Press F1 any time for the shortcut list. Ctrl+1, Ctrl+2 and Ctrl+3 jump between Generate, Gallery and Online Gallery, and Ctrl+, opens Settings. Every shortcut can be remapped in Settings.",
  "@tips_studio_guide_7": {
    "description": "Default shortcuts: showShortcutHelp f1, navigateTo* ctrl+1/2/3, settings ctrl+comma."
  },
  "tips_studio_guide_8": "Worried about burning a pile of Anlas by accident? Turn on the High Anlas cost warning in Settings, and any generation estimated above your threshold will ask before it runs.",
  "@tips_studio_guide_8": {
    "description": "settings_warnHighAnlasCostTitle."
  },
  "tips_studio_trick_1": "The seed decides which image you pull. Same settings plus the same seed means the same picture. Want to recreate a masterpiece? Keep the seed. Want new luck? Stop staring at that seed.",
  "@tips_studio_trick_1": {
    "description": "NovelAI output is deterministic for identical parameters and seed."
  },
  "tips_studio_trick_2": "Reusing a pre-encoded Vibe skips the 2 Anlas encoding fee. Two Anlas doesn't sound like much — until you count how many Vibes you use in a day.",
  "@tips_studio_trick_2": {
    "description": "drop_reuseVibeSubtitle / drop_useAsRawImageSubtitle."
  },
  "tips_studio_trick_3": "Undesired Content isn't a wishing well. Writing \"bad hands\" a hundred times does less than describing the hands clearly in the prompt. Leave the usual boilerplate to the Undesired Content preset.",
  "@tips_studio_trick_3": {
    "description": "UC preset selector on the negative tab (ucPreset_label)."
  },
  "tips_studio_trick_4": "Longer artist strings aren't always better. Past ten names, the model probably can't tell whose brushwork you actually want. Split them into a few blocks and let random draws rotate them in.",
  "@tips_studio_trick_4": {
    "description": "Random draw block mode."
  },
  "tips_studio_trick_5": "Requests per click and images per request are two different numbers. The button shows the total, and Anlas is charged on the total too. Check before you click. Don't ask how I know.",
  "@tips_studio_trick_5": {
    "description": "Button count = nSamples x imagesPerRequest; estimatedCost uses both."
  },
  "tips_studio_trick_6": "Middle-click a translation block to flip between the original and the translation. However good the AI is, peek at the original now and then to make sure \"cat ears\" didn't become something strange.",
  "@tips_studio_trick_6": {
    "description": "promptTranslation_guideMiddleText."
  },
  "tips_studio_trick_7": "Limit generation frequency in Settings forces a cooldown between runs, and a little random jitter keeps the rhythm from feeling mechanical. Good for slow late-night sessions — and for anyone whose finger won't leave the button.",
  "@tips_studio_trick_7": {
    "description": "settings_limitGenerationIntervalTitle / settings_setGenerationIntervalJitterTitle."
  },
  "tips_studio_wolf_1": "Welcome to the den. I carry the images you make back here and stack them neatly in the gallery. Honestly, I'm far better at tidying than at drawing.",
  "tips_studio_wolf_2": "Wolves see best at night. So if you're still here at 3 a.m., I won't say a word. I'll just keep you company for one more pull.",
  "tips_studio_wolf_3": "They say an AI artist comes of age the first time they count the fingers on one hand without panicking. I don't have fingers, so I've always been calm.",
  "tips_studio_wolf_4": "Pack rules: share good seeds, save good prompts as blocks, and save good images before you admire them. The last one matters most. Don't ask why.",
  "tips_studio_wolf_5": "I can't draw, but I'm very good at waiting. Those few seconds when the live preview slowly sharpens are the quietest part of my day.",
  "tips_studio_wolf_6": "W.O.F stands for WolF. As for the dots in between? Those are my paw prints in the snow.",
  "tips_studio_wolf_7": "When the canvas is empty, I curl up here for a nap. Hit Generate and I'm awake.",
  "tips_studio_night_1": "It's the middle of the night. Friendly reminder: your taste runs about 30% bolder at this hour. Take another look in the morning.",
  "tips_studio_night_2": "It's late, and somewhere in a server room a GPU just yawned. Finish this batch and get some sleep. I'll guard the gallery.",
  "tips_lab_guide_1": "Style Explore is an audition. Start an explore run to lock in the prompt and settings, then generate a batch of candidates. The children you pick become the next generation's parents, and the style moves toward what you want one generation at a time.",
  "@tips_lab_guide_1": {
    "description": "Explore runs snapshot prompt and parameters; branches turn picked children into parents."
  },
  "tips_lab_guide_2": "Hearts and folders are for your own organizing; they don't affect inheritance. What decides the next generation is the set you pick with \"Select for branch.\"",
  "@tips_lab_guide_2": {
    "description": "Heart/folder are annotations only (explore_candidate_gallery); styleExplore_branchSelect."
  },
  "tips_lab_guide_3": "Cannot decide? Use the A/B comparison: two parent images appear side by side and you only answer which is closer to the style you want. Parents ranked higher are more likely to get children next round.",
  "@tips_lab_guide_3": {
    "description": "Preference values weight parent selection in ExploreMutationEngine."
  },
  "tips_lab_guide_4": "To generate the next round, the main prompt needs at least one random block with evolution enabled. No variable genes, nothing for the mutation engine to work with.",
  "@tips_lab_guide_4": {
    "description": "styleExplore_deepRoundNoInstance."
  },
  "tips_lab_guide_5": "Found a candidate with a great combination? Adopt as block saves it to the block library so you can use it on the Generate page too. Select several and Merge & adopt combines them into one block.",
  "@tips_lab_guide_5": {
    "description": "styleExplore_adoptAsBlock / styleExplore_mergeAdopt."
  },
  "tips_lab_guide_6": "Deleting an explore run only removes the candidate copies in its run folder; originals in the gallery stay untouched. Clean up freely — a lab is supposed to be a bit messy.",
  "@tips_lab_guide_6": {
    "description": "styleExplore_deleteRunMessage."
  },
  "tips_lab_trick_1": "Every parent is guaranteed at least one child per round, so more parents means more images per round. Get greedy and your Anlas will call time for you.",
  "@tips_lab_trick_1": {
    "description": "styleExplore_deepRoundCountHint."
  },
  "tips_lab_trick_2": "You can only branch from the latest generation's pile. You can look back, but you can't fork from halfway. Evolution is ruthless like that.",
  "@tips_lab_trick_2": {
    "description": "styleExplore_branchNeedLatest."
  },
  "tips_lab_trick_3": "Sometimes the mutation engine says it can't produce enough distinct children. It isn't slacking — the gene pool is just too small. Add a few more options to the random block and it gets right back to work.",
  "@tips_lab_trick_3": {
    "description": "styleExplore_deepRoundEmpty; injection draws new atoms from the block pool."
  },
  "tips_lab_trick_4": "Hover a thumbnail in the candidate pile to see it large. No need to open them one by one; a judge has to be efficient.",
  "@tips_lab_trick_4": {
    "description": "Pile thumbnail hover preview (ExploreCandidateHoverSession)."
  },
  "tips_lab_trick_5": "Like a candidate's whole setup? Import metadata moves its prompt and settings straight back into the editor so you can keep tweaking from there.",
  "@tips_lab_trick_5": {
    "description": "styleExplore_fixateAsTemplate."
  },
  "tips_lab_wolf_1": "No wolf is born the strongest in the pack. Styles are the same: a rough first generation is normal. Judge it at the third.",
  "tips_lab_wolf_2": "Survival of the fittest has a gentle version here: candidates you don't pick don't disappear. It just wasn't their turn this round.",
  "tips_lab_wolf_3": "My entire understanding of genetics: good-looking parents usually have good-looking pups. The rest is mutation and a little luck.",
  "tips_lab_wolf_4": "The lights in the LAB usually stay on late. I'm on duty at the door, keeping count of which generation we're on.",
  "tips_lab_wolf_5": "Never underestimate mutation. Sometimes the thing you couldn't find in ten generations shows up by accident. So don't rush to delete the one that looks off.",
  "tips_prompt_guide_1": "Ctrl+Enter generates; Esc cancels a run in progress.",
  "@tips_prompt_guide_1": {
    "description": "Shortcuts generateImage ctrl+enter / cancelGeneration escape (web_style_layout)."
  },
  "tips_prompt_guide_2": "Select some text and hold Alt while scrolling to change its weight. Without Alt, the wheel just scrolls.",
  "@tips_prompt_guide_2": {
    "description": "Weight scroll modifier (default Alt)."
  },
  "tips_prompt_guide_3": "Ctrl+click a tag to look it up in the local tag library; Ctrl+drag across a phrase to see tags that often appear with it.",
  "@tips_prompt_guide_3": {
    "description": "prompt_cooccurrenceRecommendationSubtitle (default on)."
  },
  "tips_prompt_guide_4": "Right-click selected text to save it straight to the block library. Next time, one click or drag brings it back.",
  "@tips_prompt_guide_4": {
    "description": "Selection context menu promptBlockLibrary_saveToLibrary."
  },
  "tips_prompt_guide_5": "The quality tag preset at the bottom of this box adds the usual quality tags for you; switch to Undesired Content and the same spot holds its preset.",
  "@tips_prompt_guide_5": {
    "description": "QualityTagsSelector / UcPresetSelector in the prompt card footer."
  },
  "tips_prompt_guide_6": "Press F1 to see every shortcut.",
  "@tips_prompt_guide_6": {
    "description": "showShortcutHelp f1."
  },
  "tips_prompt_guide_7": "Paste a multi-character prompt copied from ComfyUI and it's recognized, with an offer to import it as character boxes — no retyping one by one.",
  "@tips_prompt_guide_7": {
    "description": "ComfyuiImportWrapper detects ComfyUI multi-character syntax."
  },
  "tips_prompt_guide_8": "With SD Syntax Auto Convert on, weights like (tag:1.2) are converted to the NovelAI format when you leave the box or generate.",
  "@tips_prompt_guide_8": {
    "description": "prompt_sdSyntaxAutoConvertSubtitle (default off)."
  },
  "tips_prompt_guide_9": "1.2::tag:: sets an exact weight; a negative number pushes the other way.",
  "@tips_prompt_guide_9": {
    "description": "NovelAI V4+ numeric emphasis syntax."
  },
  "tips_prompt_trick_1": "Each layer of curly braces multiplies the weight by 1.05; each layer of square brackets divides it by 1.05. Anyone wrapping five layers of braces is usually arguing with the model.",
  "@tips_prompt_trick_1": {
    "description": "NovelAI bracket emphasis."
  },
  "tips_prompt_trick_2": "Auto Format strips useless 1.0 weights. It isn't judging you; it's saving tokens.",
  "@tips_prompt_trick_2": {
    "description": "prompt_autoFormatSubtitle (default on)."
  },
  "tips_prompt_trick_3": "The thin bar at the bottom shows token usage. Once it's full, the model barely sees anything past it. If you're writing a novel, this isn't the place.",
  "@tips_prompt_trick_3": {
    "description": "PromptTokenCountFooter."
  },
  "tips_prompt_trick_4": "Stuck? Start with the biggest thing in the picture.",
  "tips_prompt_trick_5": "One set of quality tags is enough. Typing masterpiece three times doesn't make you look more sincere to the model.",
  "tips_prompt_trick_6": "Want something present but not stealing the show? 0.8:: works better than deleting it. Deleting means gone; lowering the weight means low-key.",
  "@tips_prompt_trick_6": {
    "description": "NovelAI numeric emphasis."
  },
  "tips_prompt_trick_7": "Swapping the same few words over and over? Make a block and let random draws do it.",
  "@tips_prompt_trick_7": {
    "description": "Random draw block mode."
  },
  "tips_prompt_trick_8": "Put what you want in the prompt and what you don't want in Undesired Content. Write \"no hat\" in the prompt and the model mostly just hears \"hat.\"",
  "tips_prompt_wolf_1": "This box has seen thousands of masterpieces, and a few things best left unshared.",
  "tips_prompt_wolf_2": "Describe the picture in one plain sentence first, then break it into tags. Do it the other way around and you often get a pile of tags and a picture nobody understands.",
  "tips_prompt_wolf_3": "I'm watching you type. Relax, I can't read.",
  "tips_prompt_wolf_4": "Somewhere far away, a GPU just sighed at your prompt.",
  "tips_prompt_wolf_5": "Gacha ends in superstition. Superstition ends in a fixed seed.",
  "tips_prompt_wolf_6": "By the twelfth artist tag, the model no longer knows whose style it's drawing. Neither do you.",
  "tips_explore_guide_1": "This is the parent prompt. To let part of it evolve, turn that part into a random block and enable evolution on the block.",
  "@tips_explore_guide_1": {
    "description": "pillCardEvolutionEnable (explore only)."
  },
  "tips_explore_guide_2": "Evolution can only be enabled once the block instance is enabled. If it's greyed out, enable the block first.",
  "@tips_explore_guide_2": {
    "description": "pillCardEvolutionRequiresEnabled."
  },
  "tips_explore_guide_3": "The number next to Generate candidates sets how many images this round makes.",
  "@tips_explore_guide_3": {
    "description": "styleExplore_createDeepRound count box."
  },
  "tips_explore_guide_4": "Block instances can step back and forward one scene at a time through the combinations they have already rolled.",
  "@tips_explore_guide_4": {
    "description": "pillCardStepBack / pillCardStepForward."
  },
  "tips_explore_guide_5": "An explore run keeps a snapshot of the prompt and settings. Editing here afterwards won't change rounds that already finished.",
  "@tips_explore_guide_5": {
    "description": "styleExplore_runEmptyHint."
  },
  "tips_explore_guide_6": "A block's random settings control draw count, trigger chance and random weight — that's where all the genetic variety lives.",
  "@tips_explore_guide_6": {
    "description": "pillCardSettings / pillSettingsCount / TriggerProbability / Weight."
  },
  "tips_explore_trick_1": "The bigger the gene pool, the more mutation has to work with. Put only two words in a random block and ten generations will just bounce between two answers.",
  "tips_explore_trick_2": "Hard-code what you're sure about and make the uncertain parts random. All random means no direction; all fixed means no evolution.",
  "tips_explore_trick_3": "Locked blocks don't get re-rolled. To keep a trait, lock it first and let the other blocks do the experimenting.",
  "@tips_explore_trick_3": {
    "description": "pillCardRerollLocked."
  },
  "tips_explore_trick_4": "Set a trigger chance of 30% and the block shows up in roughly three out of ten combinations — great for touches that only look good once in a while.",
  "@tips_explore_trick_4": {
    "description": "pillSettingsTriggerProbability."
  },
  "tips_explore_trick_5": "Expecting perfection in the first generation? That's called wishing, not exploring.",
  "tips_explore_wolf_1": "A pack's bloodline is chosen one generation at a time. So is your style.",
  "tips_explore_wolf_2": "Every round is an open audition with exactly one judge: you. I'm in charge of applause.",
  "tips_explore_wolf_3": "Good genes come from good parents. Good parents come from that one click where your hand didn't slip.",
  "tips_explore_wolf_4": "I don't know much genetics, but I know this: picky judges raise the best-looking pups.",
  "tips_character_guide_1": "A character box is really a placement box: cats, lamps, signs — it doesn't have to be a person.",
  "@tips_character_guide_1": {
    "description": "Character prompts carry a position; content is free-form."
  },
  "tips_character_guide_2": "Switch Position above to Custom, then drag the anchor on the preview. It applies when you let go.",
  "@tips_character_guide_2": {
    "description": "CharacterPositionModeSegments / characterCanvas_dragHint."
  },
  "tips_character_guide_3": "AI's Choice lets the model handle placement. Switch back to Custom and your earlier positions are still there.",
  "@tips_character_guide_3": {
    "description": "AI choice hides anchors but keeps position data (character_position_canvas)."
  },
  "tips_character_guide_4": "Every character box has its own Undesired Content tab that only applies to that character.",
  "@tips_character_guide_4": {
    "description": "CharacterPromptEditor negative tab."
  },
  "tips_character_guide_5": "The check mark at the top right disables this character for now — no need to delete and retype.",
  "@tips_character_guide_5": {
    "description": "toggleCharacterEnabled header button."
  },
  "tips_character_guide_6": "Click the title to rename this character. Much easier to tell apart than numbers.",
  "@tips_character_guide_6": {
    "description": "CharacterNameField."
  },
  "tips_character_guide_7": "Use the ⋯ menu at the top right to add this character to the block library and reuse its description later.",
  "@tips_character_guide_7": {
    "description": "Character header menu addToLibrary."
  },
  "tips_character_trick_1": "Keep scene and style in the main prompt and only this character here. Write an outfit twice and the model assumes you love it.",
  "tips_character_trick_2": "Two people placed too close tend to merge. Pulling their anchors apart works better than writing \"separate\" ten times.",
  "tips_character_trick_3": "Want a tree on the left? Give it a character box and drag it there. The tree won't complain about not being a character.",
  "tips_character_trick_4": "Blocks and weight syntax work in character boxes too, just like the main prompt.",
  "@tips_character_trick_4": {
    "description": "Character boxes use PromptPillEditor."
  },
  "tips_character_trick_5": "Too many characters? Disable a few. In a crowded frame the model picks who stays — usually not the one you wanted.",
  "tips_character_wolf_1": "I'd like a character box too, but I think I'm better off watching from outside the frame.",
  "tips_character_wolf_2": "One box, one place, one job. Sounds like a good philosophy for life.",
  "tips_character_wolf_3": "You handle the blocking; I'll stand on the side yelling \"a little more to the left.\"",
  "tips_character_wolf_4": "Even a wolf pack moves in formation. With lots of characters, decide who stands in the middle first.",
